  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5003",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to ME-180 through a series of molecular interactions that involve different targets. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin may act through multiple pathways, with ME-180 being a downstream target in each of these routes. In Path 1, doxorubicin targets KM12, which in turn targets ME-180. In Path 2, doxorubicin targets a probable G-protein coupled receptor 132, which is targeted by Racotumomab, and this same receptor is also targeted by ME-180. In Path 3, doxorubicin targets COLO-792, which is targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which ultimately targets ME-180. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which doxorubicin influences ME-180, possibly through receptor activation or metabolic modulation. The integration of these evidence points suggests that ME-180 may be a downstream effector in the signaling cascade initiated by doxorubicin, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
